findings.body:
The PR changes `WryWebviewDispatcher::delete_cookie` to send `WebviewMessage::SetCookie`. The `set_cookie` method right above it already sends `SetCookie`, so the two are now identical. Calling `Webview::delete_cookie` will therefore set the cookie in the native store rather than remove it. The event loop still has a separate `DeleteCookie` arm at `crates/tauri-runtime-wry/src/lib.rs` around line 3737, so that path is now unreachable from the public API.

::diff{file="crates/tauri-runtime-wry/src/lib.rs" lines="1714-1720"}

The original code sent `DeleteCookie`, so the intended fix was to keep `DeleteCookie` and only drop the redundant clone (`cookie.into_owned()` without `.clone()`). The diff's change to `SetCookie` looks like an accidental edit. There is also no test covering `delete_cookie`, which is why this went unnoticed.

`WebviewWindowBuilder::with_window_features` is public and is removed in this diff. Any downstream code calling it will fail to compile. The rename is a bigger change than the three regressions the PR describes, and it isn't mentioned in the PR description.

::diff{file="crates/tauri/src/webview/webview_window.rs" lines="1315-1321"}

If the rename is intended, keep the old name as a `#[deprecated]` alias for a release cycle so callers get a warning rather than a compile error. If the old name never shipped in a release, say so in the PR description so reviewers can confirm the break is acceptable. The doc examples in `mod.rs` and the example app are updated correctly.

The edited body has irregular spacing: `inner_size(size.width,    size.height)` has four spaces, and `position(position.x,position.y)` has none. `cargo fmt --check` will fail, which breaks the repo's CI lint step.

::diff{file="crates/tauri/src/webview/webview_window.rs" lines="1316-1321"}

In addition, the diff swaps the order of the `position` and `inner_size` calls without explanation. The result is probably the same, but reviewers should confirm that the order doesn't matter on any platform.
